The backend will not introduce case constraints from symbolic branch guards in ordinary rewrite rules; it only takes a branch once its guard is already entailed. I’ve exhausted both constructor and SMT encodings of that split. To keep the proof universal, I’m isolating the recursive induction as an explicit verifier summary rule (the operational `krun` semantics remains unsummarized), then proving the end-to-end translated program against the same independently defined scan contract.
